Use this as the complete `.gitignore`:

```gitignore
# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example

# Python / backend
.venv/
backend/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Node / Next.js
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
coverage/
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*

# Generated app files
backend/exports/
backend/screenshots/
backend/snapshots/

# Local databases
backend/*.db
backend/*.sqlite
backend/*.sqlite3

# Celery
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# Docker local data
postgres-data/

# Deployment / platform metadata
.vercel/

# v0 sandbox internal files
__v0_runtime_loader.js
__v0_devtools.tsx
__v0_jsx-dev-runtime.ts
.snowflake/
.v0-trash/

# macOS
.DS_Store
```
